            "collusion",
            "corroborate",
            "convivial",
            "coherent",
            "compassionate",
            "colloquial"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on con- and its shapes."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "root": "syn"
        },
        "cap": "Greek syn- (together)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>consensus</b><br>general agreement",
            "<b>con-</b> <i>together</i> + sens <i>feel</i><br>→ “feeling together”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>concur</b><br>to agree",
            "<b>con-</b> <i>together</i> + cur <i>run</i><br>→ “run together”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>congregate</b><br>to gather into a crowd or group",
            "<b>con-</b> <i>together</i> + greg <i>flock</i> + -ate<br>→ “flock together”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>contemporary</b><br>living or happening at the same time; also, modern",
            "<b>con-</b> <i>with</i> + tempor <i>time</i> + -ary<br>→ “of the same time”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>collusion</b><br>secret cooperation for a dishonest purpose",
            "<b>col-</b> <i>together</i> + lus <i>play</i> + -ion<br>→ “playing together (in secret)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>corroborate</b><br>to confirm with more evidence",
            "<b>cor-</b> <i>together</i> + robor <i>strength</i> + -ate<br>→ “strengthen together”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>convivial</b><br>friendly and lively; fond of good company",
            "<b>con-</b> <i>together</i> + viv <i>live</i> + -ial<br>→ “living (feasting) together”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>synchronize</b><br>to make things happen at the same time",
            "<b>syn-</b> <i>together</i> + chron <i>time</i> + -ize<br>→ “make the same time”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>sympathy</i></b><br>sharing or understanding another’s sorrow",
            "<b>sym-</b> <i>with</i> + path <i>feeling</i> + -y<br>→ “feeling with”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts. Words in italics are familiar words that are not on the list."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "The nurse was <b>compassionate</b>, gentle with every frightened patient. What does <i>compassionate</i> mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>com-</b> (with) + <b>passion</b> (suffering, as in the older sense of the word) + <b>-ate</b>.",
          "Literally: “suffering with” someone.",
          "The sentence fits: she felt for her patients."
        ],
        "a": "Feeling for others’ suffering and wanting to help."
      },
